{"title":"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#An_alternate_way_to_start\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">An alternate way to start</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2.1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fast_And_Clean)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fast And Clean)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In how many ways can <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c72d8d34783d3db7b917c953ca22225f513823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$345$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> be written as the sum of an increasing sequence of two or more consecutive positive integers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fbae31ce1e7a9e307bbeab198ed0f576ef22fdfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff35bddba45a1a680b7ed74c1347a411fc2a9c0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$345=3\\cdot 5\\cdot 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose we take an odd number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of consecutive integers, with the median as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0e61647f7f44b877e66e4f048fc6e848e7f6f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$mk=345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fb76ee2a149144ec5474fe396b4ae74152dc37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac12k&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"60\" height=\"21\" />.\nLooking at the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c72d8d34783d3db7b917c953ca22225f513823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$345$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/7198e25f6a2fb001dac0d33f8aa79f35c7de8398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,5,15,23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> with medians as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999bd4a29982209088c71cb05dabf9ffd64be5c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$115,69,23,15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Suppose instead we take an even number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> of consecutive integers, with median being the average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4bea4f5ee837b0249288558f2fb73a871b264491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a24d60aeb830512c16869d95b8ab0fea73d0094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(2m+1)=345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638e49317f9ad329e712720071b8e8129edaa7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ &lt; m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />.\nLooking again at the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c72d8d34783d3db7b917c953ca22225f513823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$345$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/97827a34a0f6699ae2b5fd23665cc8eecd056286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> with medians <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f5fde636d19a9b53abfcf3f4929a4f2e5fefd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(172,173),(57,58),(34,35)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db8297beb63746f6ff2048545ae337e3b0962ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\nMinor changes by Masorge\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need to find consecutive numbers (an arithmetic sequence that increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) that sums to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c72d8d34783d3db7b917c953ca22225f513823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$345$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. This calls for the sum of an arithmetic sequence given that the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the last term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> elements, which is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53cf328e08bf502e78c91b5f9a8bd5e7e29f658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {n \\cdot (k+g)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We look for sequences of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> consecutive numbers starting at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and ending at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/769df4aeb46799be3d2b5b0f7de9dd2730f9d51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. We can now substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/769df4aeb46799be3d2b5b0f7de9dd2730f9d51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Now we substitute our new value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53cf328e08bf502e78c91b5f9a8bd5e7e29f658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {n \\cdot (k+g)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> to get that the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/6206664cd7e799bd7c43ea52dd11b9374d4ca02f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {n \\cdot (k+k+n-1)}{2} = 345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"199\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7eb49b7959432ae00ab1090f9e064aab0b514a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {n \\cdot (2k+n-1)}{2} = 345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"176\" height=\"38\" />. This gives a nice equation. We multiply out the 2 to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/75261dc9042ee0c6393aebbadece6780f4c211ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot (2k+n-1)=690$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />. This leaves us with 2 integers that multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd2065782067101d1311681df1de20f0e1a7af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$690$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> which leads us to think of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd2065782067101d1311681df1de20f0e1a7af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$690$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. We know the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd2065782067101d1311681df1de20f0e1a7af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$690$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> are:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/2209015cd2ab1990adf3ab485721173623e32541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3,5,6,10,15,23,30,46,69,115,138,230,345,690$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"411\" height=\"16\" />. So through inspection (checking), we see that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed6fbfb69662bc3183ac8828e10a7eed255b80b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,3,5,6,10,15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> work. This gives us the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db8297beb63746f6ff2048545ae337e3b0962ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> ways.\n</p><p>~~jk23541\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"An_alternate_way_to_start\">An alternate way to start</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: An alternate way to start\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the sequence have \\(k\\) terms starting from a positive integer \\(a\\). The sum of this sequence is given by the arithmetic series formula:\\(S=\\frac{k}{2}[2a+(k-1)]\\)We are given \\(S = 345\\), with the constraints \\(k \\geq 2\\) and \\(a \\geq 1\\). Multiplying both sides by \\(2\\) gives:\\(2\\times 345=k(2a+k-1)\\)\\(690=k(2a+k-1)\\)\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288#Created_Pages\" title=\"User：Icosahedron0288\">Icosahedron0288</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>An alternate way to finish.\n</p><p>Let \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e787ef4775d22cb112ed54d2abdb402f11195eed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2k+n-1 &amp;=\\frac{690}{k} \\\\ n &amp;= k \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"136\" height=\"58\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b761c7efc5143cc1c0b31ebfc9846dae8af43c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$690.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />\nWe find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2c96d9dd2406c7830f3abca8f678563af44ee2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k = 1+\\frac{690}{k}-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"137\" height=\"37\" /> so we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb1b1ac45af3f10166e2f9302a25daa7630f952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{690}{k} - k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" /> to be positive and odd. Fortunately, regardless of the parity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb1b1ac45af3f10166e2f9302a25daa7630f952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{690}{k} - k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" /> is odd. Furthermore, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45c224e5582a70369e80d2ddaf8d7cbea0ff7a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{690}{k} &gt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" /> which eliminates exact half of the factors. Now, since we need more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integer to sum up we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> which eliminates one more case. There were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases to begin with, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/4214057e8e11842f1b7ffea866fa816d2efb69d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{2}-1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"132\" height=\"37\" /> ways.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2.1\">Solution 2.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the very end of Solution 2, where we find the factors of 690, instead of inspection, notice that all numbers will work until you get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and that is because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d879e96ce42b1fab36f2377af5c8a2223f2446fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{345}{30}=11.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must be the middle 2 numbers; however, a sequence of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> with middle numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> that consists only of integers would go into the negatives, so any number from 30 onwards wouldn't work, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a trivial, non-counted solution, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db8297beb63746f6ff2048545ae337e3b0962ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> -ColtsFan10\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fast_And_Clean.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fast_And_Clean)\">Solution 3 (Fast And Clean)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fast And Clean)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The median of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is either an integer or a half integer. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476753b612643739f95b780b84a76aca181fc5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=\\frac{i}{2}, i \\in N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"39\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d9aa5fd0542e625cad1f9438fa8e7b75bbde74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=i\\cdot n=2\\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"180\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>On the other hand we have two constraints: \n</p><p>1) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d7451d4690269e0ecb0700b51c980d03a83b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\geq \\frac{n+1}{2} \\iff i&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" /> because the integers in the sequence are all positive, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />;\n</p><p>2) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is even; if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a half integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is odd. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> have opposite parity.\n</p><p>Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> factors and it is not a perfect square. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb565cb8cd6a6236d4de94f7d55238e0ae60870a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8-1=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/3585847d4103f526f77b6537874436d050a2d93b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; n &lt; \\sqrt{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" />. Also since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/9629413a976dea9cf5d1b79976e47f92abe426b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2|P, 4\\nmid P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59fea99070ce96abf13dbf140685f741786286fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{P}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"39\" /> must have opposite parity. Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db8297beb63746f6ff2048545ae337e3b0962ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ asops\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can find consecutive ways by checking individual numbers. For example, if you want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive numbers to add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c72d8d34783d3db7b917c953ca22225f513823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$345$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, you can set up \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04ab4573c4bef66205b21566a3143cfe07971b04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} a+(a+1) &amp;=345 \\\\ 2a+1 &amp;=345 \\\\ 2a &amp;= 344 \\\\ a &amp;= 172 \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"88\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1eef0695d030238375b13b59dcf8ee1b8ca04b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$172+173=345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> you would do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/d/68d65f83fb258f1a54c8e0a5055da616c162275e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1)+a+(a+1)+(a+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"243\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81f0316ce7fe26ba901760573416248d5fdcd47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> it would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/2924e5de1fd4a1a2fd884d438c6883627e98c257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6a+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, so for any even number it would be in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/7071292e0dd05651369ea44c6b6cbdb48aaf1424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ka+\\frac{k}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"39\" />. For all multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> you can rule out since they are dividing by an even number after taking away an even number, and 345 is odd so it would not turn out to be a whole number.\n</p><p>For odd numbers it will center around the middle. Take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as an example:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/2229a3e79343c028a26a0c15913bd24f873df404.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split} (a-1)+a+(a+1) &amp;=345 \\\\ 3a &amp;=345 \\\\ a &amp;= 115 \\end{split}\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"63\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/2792e2f78905a7dd85316f46bac98966d2f52e6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$114+115+116=345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"180\" height=\"15\" />. You can see that for odd numbers that if you put <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in the middle all the numbers will cancel out and become the center number. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> it would just be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f1cd011e4f743ca6187ecad0222dce00a68993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5a$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />. For all odd numbers it will just be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408730e185e0b41fcc93fd334b48e79f1c8e799d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ka$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Using this method and testing you will find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed6fbfb69662bc3183ac8828e10a7eed255b80b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,3,5,6,10,15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> work. At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> you will notice that the center is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and that the first number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so by intuition you are done. On top of that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the highest possible answer so with certainty you can say that you're answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/62710b1a623ded8eb77840a8ae5bcdcf62eefce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"50\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dwEm_PcmaYg\">https://youtu.be/dwEm_PcmaYg</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZhAZ1oPe5Ds?t=950\">https://youtu.be/ZhAZ1oPe5Ds?t=950</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B\">2016 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=